  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When a unit of demand is short in a quarter and finally delivered in a later quarter, is the delay compensation charged for every quarter from the original due quarter up to and including the delivery quarter (so a Q1 demand delivered in Q3 incurs 3 quarters of compensation), or only for the quarters it was actually short before delivery (so the same case incurs 2 quarters of compensation)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice between two mutually exclusive calculation methods for delay compensation."
}

